// Silent exit progress/contact diagnostic, revision 37,105, 50-field frame.
// Preserve approach, positioning, pivot, powers and sensor configuration.
// Require BOTH sampled motor totals >=180, THEN five consecutive both-black
// samples, and both-black again after braking. Reason16 means this bounded
// criterion passed, NOT exact alignment, track containment or route success.
// A lone moving track, persistent one-sided contact, or zero progress cannot
// pass. Reason15 means the criterion was not established within the watchdog.
// 180 is an experimental motor-count reference, NOT body degrees/distance.
// 200 intervals is only a safety watchdog, never the completion criterion.
// The larger watchdog permits observing whether correction actually returns
// to both-black beyond the old100 cutoff; sampled readings may affect timing.
// White/loss/encoder fault stops remain; no second turn, search or sound.
#define CORNER_REVISION 105
#define EXIT_STEPS 200
#define EXIT_FORWARD_POWER 12
#define EXIT_CORRECTION_POWER 9
#define EXIT_MEASURE_ENCODERS 1
#define EXIT_REQUIRE_PROGRESS 1
#define EXIT_PROGRESS_TARGET 180
#define EXIT_CENTER_SAMPLES 5
#include "robot_prueba_codo.nxc"
